# Spine — Project Knowledge Base
> This file gives Cursor (and any AI assistant) full context about the Spine project.
> Keep it updated as the project grows.

---

## What is Spine?

Spine is a cross-platform book reading social app for iOS, Android, and Web. It lets users track books they've read, are reading, and want to read — with a social layer built around friends, book clubs, and shared reading experiences.

**Core pillars:**
1. **Library** — personal shelf with reading progress, ratings, and reviews
2. **Discover** — AI-powered + friend-influenced book recommendations
3. **Social** — friends, activity feed, see what your circle is reading
4. **Clubs** — book clubs with real-time chat, finish-gated spoiler channels, and group reading progress
5. **Gamification** — XP, levels, badges, reading streaks, yearly challenges

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Mobile + Web | **Expo (React Native)** via `expo-router` | One codebase for iOS, Android, web |
| Backend / DB | **Supabase** (PostgreSQL) | Auth, real-time, RLS, storage |
| State | **Zustand** | Auth state, local library cache |
| Server state | **TanStack React Query** | Data fetching, caching, refetch |
| Book data | **Open Library API** | Free, no key, millions of titles |
| Language | **TypeScript** | Strict types throughout |
| iOS builds | **EAS Build** (Expo cloud) | No Mac needed for iOS builds |
| Testing (dev) | **Expo Go** | Scan QR, runs on real device instantly |

