## Database Schema (Supabase / PostgreSQL)

### Tables

**`profiles`** — extends `auth.users`
- `id` (UUID, FK to auth.users)
- `username` (unique)
- `display_name`
- `avatar_url`
- `bio`
- `reading_goal` (int, books/year, default 12)
- `xp`, `level`, `streak_days`
- `last_read_at`
- Auto-created on signup via DB trigger

**`books`** — cached from Open Library / Google Books
- `id` (UUID)
- `open_library_id`, `google_books_id`, `isbn`
- `title`, `author`, `description`
- `cover_url`, `genres[]`, `page_count`, `published_year`
- Books are upserted on first user interaction, not pre-populated

**`user_books`** — a user's shelf entry for a book
- `user_id`, `book_id`
- `status`: `want | reading | read | did_not_finish`
- `rating` (0.0–5.0, half-star increments), `review`
- `progress_page`, `started_at`, `finished_at`
- Unique constraint: `(user_id, book_id)`

**`friendships`**
- `requester`, `addressee` (both UUID → profiles)
- `status`: `pending | accepted | blocked`
- View `friends` provides bidirectional pairs for easy querying

**`clubs`**
- `name`, `description`, `cover_color`
- `is_private`, `invite_code`
- `current_book_id`, `next_meeting`
- `created_by`

**`club_members`** — junction: `(club_id, user_id, role)`
- `role`: `owner | admin | member`

**`club_messages`** — real-time chat
- `club_id`, `user_id`, `content`
- `channel`: `reading | finished` (for spoiler gate)
- `book_id`, `chapter` (optional, for chapter-tagged messages)
- Realtime enabled via `supabase_realtime` publication

**`activities`** — denormalized feed events
- `type`: `started_reading | finished_book | rated_book | added_to_shelf | joined_club | earned_badge`
- `book_id`, `club_id`, `metadata` (JSONB)
- Realtime enabled

**`badges`** + **`user_badges`**
- Badges seeded: `first_book`, `speed_reader`, `genre_explorer`, `social_butterfly`, `centurion`, `streak_30`, `club_founder`, `critic`

**`club_book_finishers`** _(planned, not yet migrated)_
- Gates access to `finished` channel in clubs
- `quiz_passed` boolean — verified via AI-generated quiz

**`club_nominations`** + **`club_votes`** _(planned)_
- For the book selection / voting feature in clubs

### Key Views
- **`friends`** — bidirectional accepted friendship pairs
- **`friend_activity`** — activities joined with profile + book data
- **`friend_popular_books`** — books your friends rated, aggregated

### Row Level Security
- All tables have RLS enabled
- Users can only write their own data
- Friends can see each other's `reading` and `read` shelf entries (not `want`)
- Club messages respect the `channel` — `finished` channel only accessible to users in `club_book_finishers`

---

## Auth Flow

1. App boots → `app/_layout.tsx` calls `supabase.auth.getSession()`
2. If session exists → `fetchProfile(user.id)` → `router.replace('/(tabs)/')`
3. If no session → `router.replace('/(auth)/login')`
4. `supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange` handles login/logout reactively
5. Profile is stored in `useAuthStore` (Zustand) and available globally

### Supabase client (`lib/supabase.ts`)
- Uses `AsyncStorage` on iOS/Android
- Uses `localStorage` (with `window` guard) on web
- `app.json` web output must be `"single"` (not `"static"`) to avoid SSR crashes

---

## State Management

### `useAuthStore` (Zustand)
```ts
profile: Profile | null
isLoading: boolean
signIn(email, password)
signUp(email, password, username, displayName)
signOut()
fetchProfile(userId)
setProfile(profile)
```

### `useLibraryStore` (Zustand)
```ts
books: UserBook[]         // local cache of user's shelf
isLoaded: boolean
setBooks(books)           // called after initial fetch
addBook(book)             // optimistic add
updateBook(id, updates)   // optimistic update
getByStatus(status)       // filter shelf by status
getByBookId(bookId)       // find shelf entry by book
```

### React Query
Used for all server data fetching. Key patterns:
```ts
// Fetch shelf
useQuery({ queryKey: ['shelf', userId], queryFn: () => getMyShelf(userId) })

// Fetch friend activity
useQuery({ queryKey: ['friendActivity'], queryFn: getFriendActivity })

// Invalidate after mutation
queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['shelf', userId] })
```

---

## API Layer (`lib/api/`)

### `books.ts`
- `searchBooks(query)` — searches Open Library, returns `Book[]`
- `upsertBook(book)` — caches book in Supabase on first interaction
- `getMyShelf(userId)` — returns `UserBook[]` with joined `book` data
- `addToShelf(userId, book, status)` — upserts book + creates shelf entry + logs activity
- `updateShelfEntry(userBookId, updates)` — update status/progress/rating
- `rateBook(userId, bookId, rating, review)` — rate + log activity

### `friends.ts`
- `sendFriendRequest(addresseeId)`
- `respondToRequest(friendshipId, accept)`
- `getFriends(userId)` — returns `Profile[]`
- `getPendingRequests()` — incoming pending requests
- `searchUsers(query)` — search by username or display name
- `getFriendActivity(limit)` — feed from `friend_activity` view
- `getFriendRecommendations(userId)` — from `friend_popular_books` view, filtered to exclude user's shelf

### Open Library API
- Base URL: `https://openlibrary.org/search.json`
- Cover images: `https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/{cover_id}-M.jpg`
- No API key required
- Books are fetched on search and cached in the `books` table on first save

