## Routing Conventions

Expo Router uses file-based routing (like Next.js).

| Path | Screen |
|---|---|
| `/` | Redirects based on auth state |
| `/(auth)/login` | Login |
| `/(auth)/signup` | Signup |
| `/(tabs)/` | Library (home tab) |
| `/(tabs)/discover` | Discover |
| `/(tabs)/friends` | Friends |
| `/(tabs)/clubs` | Clubs list |
| `/(tabs)/profile` | Profile |
| `/book/[id]` | Book detail (book UUID) |
| `/club/[id]` | Club detail + chat (club UUID) |
| `/search` | Book search _(not yet built)_ |

Navigation:
```ts
router.push('/book/some-uuid')
router.replace('/(tabs)/')
router.back()
<Link href="/(auth)/signup" />
```

---

## Component Conventions

- All screens use `<SafeAreaView edges={['top']}>` from `react-native-safe-area-context`
- Styles always defined with `StyleSheet.create()` at the bottom of the file
- Design tokens from `constants/colors.ts` — never hardcode colors
- Screen titles use `fontFamily: 'Georgia'` for the literary aesthetic
- Loading states: `<ActivityIndicator color={COLORS.primary} />`
- Empty states: emoji + message + CTA button pattern

---

## Running the Project

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start dev server
npx expo start

# Then:
# Press w → open in browser
# Press a → open Android emulator
# Scan QR → open in Expo Go on iPhone (no Apple account needed)
```

Required `.env.local` in project root:
```
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
```

---

## EAS Build (iOS without a Mac)

```bash
# First time setup
npm install -g eas-cli
eas login
eas build:configure

# Trigger iOS build (Expo builds in the cloud)
eas build --platform ios --profile development

# Over-the-air update (skip App Store review for JS changes)
eas update --branch production --message "Fix bug"
```

EAS uses Expo's Mac servers to compile the iOS binary. You need an Apple Developer account ($99/yr) only when distributing via TestFlight or the App Store. For daily development, Expo Go is sufficient.

